Subject: Reflective KV Cache
Description: Fork-local architecture note for making KV cache address typed semantic and transformer-structural references, not only raw token-derived key/value tensors.

& [ReflectiveKVCache] is the proposed extension of Ollama's cache model
  + [source_specification] is C:\Project\ReasoningFramework\platform\source_documents\2026-05-31_ollama_reflective_kv_cache\Canonical_Reflective_KV_Cache_Specification.sop
  + [implementation_package] is kvcache
  + [first_slice] is typed reference records and validation only

  + [reference_layer] is one of surface, subtext, contract, structural, or reflective
    + [surface] is literal token-span context
    + [subtext] is typed interpretive state such as tone, implication, ambiguity, or authority tension
    + [contract] is durable rule or obligation identity such as an SOP contract
    + [structural] is subject, file, dependency, provenance, or runtime structure identity
    + [reflective] is transformer-internal parameter or activation address identity

  + [parameter_address] is a stable runtime address into a transformer tensor
    + [layer] is the transformer layer index
    + [module] is the owning runtime module or projection name
    + [tensor] is the tensor name
    + [offset] is the flattened tensor start index
    + [size] is the number of addressed scalar values

  + [activation_address] is a stable runtime address into layer/head/channel activation state
    + [layer] is the transformer layer index
    + [head] is the attention head index
    + [begin] is the first addressed channel
    + [end] is the exclusive addressed channel bound

  = must: keep current inference behavior unchanged in the first slice
  = must: validate references before any future runtime resolver consumes them
  = must: produce stable keys so typed references can later be joined, indexed, or compared
  = must: preserve exact source text outside this cache layer when exact recall matters
  - never: claim KV-cache reduction or accuracy preservation until benchmarked
